 "input": {
  "kind": "text",
  "text": "Chocolate Ice Cream\nMakes about 1 quart\n\nCustard base\n2 cups heavy cream, divided\n1 cup whole milk\n2/3 cup sugar\n5 egg yolks\n1/3 cup cocoa powder\n4 oz bittersweet chocolate, chopped\n\nTo finish\n1 tsp vanilla extract\n1/2 cup chopped toasted almonds (optional)\n\nPut the chocolate in a large bowl with 1 cup of the cream.\nHeat the milk, the remaining 1 cup cream, cocoa and sugar until steaming.\nWhisk the yolks, then slowly whisk in the hot milk mixture and return it to the pan. Cook, stirring, until it coats a spoon.\nStrain the custard base over the chocolate and cream, stir until smooth, add the vanilla and chill at least 4 hours.\nChurn the chilled base, folding in the almonds at the end if using."
 },
